310 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 165 0 R
/T (This FPGA-based group project was completed as the first assignment for a core unit \(MTRX3700: Mechatronics 3\). The project involved designing and implementing a Whac-A-Mole game on an FPGA board \(DE2-115\) using Verilog. The system replicates the classic arcade game by lighting LEDs as moles and detecting user inputs through toggle switches to register hits and misses. The game logic, timing, and scoring were handled entirely in hardware to achieve low-latency and deterministic performance. My contribution in the project was the FSM design, which coordinated all gameplay states, timing signals, and control outputs.)
/E (This FPGA-based group project was completed as the first assignment for a core unit \(MTRX3700: Mechatronics 3\). The project involved designing and implementing a Whac-A-Mole game on an FPGA board \(DE2-115\) using Verilog. The system replicates the classic arcade game by lighting LEDs as moles and detecting user inputs through toggle switches to register hits and misses. The game logic, timing, and scoring were handled entirely in hardware to achieve low-latency and deterministic performance. My contribution in the project was the FSM design, which coordinated all gameplay states, timing signals, and control outputs.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
