/Title (The Precharge Circuit is a safety-critical subsystem responsible for managing the initial connection between the accumulator and inverter in an electric vehicle. It limits inrush current during startup and ensures the tractive system voltage rises smoothly to over 95% of the accumulator voltage before the positive isolation relay closes, bypassing the precharge resistor and passing full power to the tractive system.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 836 0 R
/Next 1010 0 R
>>
endobj
